  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Under Fang Yuan’s pressure on the variant human alliance, Golden Fur Immortal Monarch, a rank eight hairy man Gu Immortal, clenches his teeth and agrees to offer his immortal aperture. He knows Fang Yuan annexed Lang Ya blessed land and rarely sent Lang Ya Sect’s hairy man Gu Immortals into battle, and he hopes for similar treatment. Hairy men are proficient in Gu refinement, which might preserve the lives of the people of Golden Fur grotto-heaven and even give them high statuses, better than being slaughtered and forcefully annexed. His agreement increases pressure on the remaining alliance members to follow.",
      "chapters": [
        2069
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_golden_fur_immortal_monarch",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "fac_lang_ya_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the Eastern Sea victory, Golden Fur Immortal Monarch kneels before Fang Yuan and proclaims that he is willing to follow him and offer his Golden Fur grotto-heaven. Cries of pledging allegiance follow, and the entire variant human alliance submits without exception.",
